            <div xml:id="d760">

                <pb facs="0986" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.00/310: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-27T14:00:00+02:35">August 27, 1935—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 27—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. In view of fantastic rumors which I understand some of the numerous foreign
                    correspondents are broadcasting for lack of something better to do I desire to
                    assure the Department that the city is perfectly calm, that no immediate
                    evacuation has been ordered either of natives or foreigners and that any
                    foreigner departing can obtain sufficient foreign exchange to take him home.
                    Many merchants are changing paper money into silver which caused mild run on the
                    bank.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
